        <title>Solution</title>
        
        <p>
          An <term>operation</term> is a mathematical action performed on the system. A
          <term>control</term> is a decision or validation drawn from a feature.
        </p>

        <tabular valign="top" top="minor">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I row reduced the augmented matrix.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I row reduced the augmented matrix.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p>None</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>Rationale</p></cell>
            <cell><p>Row reduction is an action performed on the matrix; nothing is drawn based on it.</p></cell>
          </row>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The bottom row is zero, so there are infinitely many solutions.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p>None</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The bottom row is zero, so there are infinitely many solutions.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>Rationale</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>Since no action was performed, there is no operation.</p>
              <p>
                A feature (the zero row) is read and used to reach a validating decision (infinitely many solutions).
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I counted two pivots.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I counted two pivots.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p>None</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>Rationale</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>
                Counting pivots is an action performed on the matrix. Although the
                resulting pivot count could later serve as a criterion, this statement
                does not use it to make a decision.
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>Column three has no pivot, so x_3 is free.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p>None</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>Column three has no pivot, so x_3 is free.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>Rationale</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>Since no action was performed, there is no operation.</p>
              <p>The criteria (no pivot in the column) is used to classify <m>x_3</m> as free.</p>
            </cell>
          </row>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I solved for x1 and x2, and that left x3 free.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I solved for x1 and x2</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>I solved for x1 and x2, and that left x3 free.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>Rationale</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>
                Solving for <c>x1</c> and <c>x2</c> is an operation. Whereas, using this result to determine that <c>x3 is free</c> is a control.
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution> -->
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-ws-01-components">
      <title>Identify Episode Components</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          For each response below, record:
          <ol>
            <li>the criterion <m>C</m>, copied <em>verbatim</em> from the student's words;</li>
            <li>the minimal link <m>I</m> sufficient to justify the step;</li>
            <li>the judgment <m>J</m>, copied <em>verbatim</em> from the student's words;</li>
            <li>whether the link is <c>explicit</c>, <c>implicit</c>, or <c>absent</c>; and</li>
            <li>whether the episode is complete.</li>
          </ol>
        </p>

        <tabular>
          <col width="7%"/>
          <col width="93%"/>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The augmented matrix has no [0 0 0 1] row, so the system</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell><p><c>is consistent.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The third column has no pivot. Therefore, x_3 is free.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>There are two pivots.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>x1 and x2 are basic variables.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The system has a free variable then the solution is not unique.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R6</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>The system is consistent, and it has infinitely-many solns.</c></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </statement>

